@startuml drift-gate
' The register's drift-detection gate: a SHA-keyed typed exception table with a
' non-vacuity floor. Colour key: input = blue · gate = amber · pass = green · fail = red

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFECB3
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #E65100

title <b>The drift gate — an omission FAILS, it does not go unnoticed</b>\n<size:11>shared/tests/consensus_change_register_gate.rs · CI matrix crate <i>shared</i></size>

start
:**Read the anchor**\n<i>docs/consensus/REGISTER_BASE</i>\n<size:10>one SHA; moves only by an explicit, reviewed edit</size>;
note right #E3F2FD
  CI already checks out <b>FULL history</b> —
  <i>.github/workflows/ci.yml:190-197</i> provisions it
  for <i>rholang/tests/normalize_oracle_provenance.rs</i>,
  which re-derives an oracle twin from git.
  <b>The precedent exists; this gate reuses it.</b>
end note

:**Enumerate the obligation set**\n<latex>\mathcal{O} = \mathrm{rev\text{-}list}(\mathrm{BASE}..\mathrm{HEAD}\ \texttt{--}\ \mathcal{P})</latex>\n<size:10><latex>\mathcal{P}</latex> = models/ · rholang/src/rust/interpreter/ ·</size>\n<size:10>rspace++/ · casper/src/ · shared/src/ · *.proto</size>;

:**Read the index**\n<i>docs/consensus/register.toml</i>\n<size:10><latex>\mathcal{E}</latex> = entry SHAs · <latex>\mathcal{X}</latex> = exempt SHAs</size>;

if (<latex>\mathcal{O} = \varnothing</latex> ?) then (yes)
  :**FAIL — NON-VACUITY FLOOR.**\nA gate that finds nothing to check\nis a gate that cannot fail.\nEither the path set or the anchor is wrong.;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (<latex>\mathcal{O} \subseteq \mathcal{E} \uplus \mathcal{X}</latex> ?) then (no)
  :**FAIL — UNREGISTERED COMMIT.**\nNames every missing SHA and\nthe consensus path it touched.;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (<latex>\mathcal{E} \cap \mathcal{X} = \varnothing</latex>\nand <latex>\mathcal{E} \uplus \mathcal{X} \subseteq \mathcal{O}</latex> ?) then (no)
  :**FAIL — the partition is not EXACT.**\nA SHA listed twice, or a SHA listed\nthat the range does not contain\n(a stale row surviving a rebase).;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:**Type-check every exemption row**;
if (every <i>reason</i> in the CLOSED enum,\nevery <i>evidence</i> non-empty and\nnaming a test or a measurement?) then (no)
  :**FAIL — UNTYPED EXEMPTION.**\nA free-text reason is a shrug.\nAdding a reason variant is a\ncode change, hence reviewed.;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:**Type-check every entry row**;
if (all SEVEN axis cells answered from\nthe closed vocabulary\n{MOVES, NO, N/A, UNVERIFIED}?) then (no)
  :**FAIL — UNANSWERED AXIS.**;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (<latex>|\{\text{cells} = \mathtt{UNVERIFIED}\}| \leq</latex> the declared budget?) then (no)
  :**FAIL — UNVERIFIED CREEP.**\nThe count is asserted EXACTLY, so\n<i>UNVERIFIED</i> is a legitimate answer\nthat cannot silently accumulate.;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (every <i>id</i> in the index appears as a\nheading in the prose register,\nand every prose heading is in the index?) then (no)
  :**FAIL — PROSE/INDEX DIVERGENCE.**;<<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:**PASS.**\nEvery consensus-path commit in range is\nEITHER an entry OR an exemption carrying\nits own discharged obligation.;<<#C8E6C9>>
stop
@enduml
